GRID | cell_px | 80
# map_cols / map_rows - real desktop-wide "movement wall" (direct
# instruction 2026-08-31: "so players cant lose the map moving stuff
# around too much"). Uncomment + set to a real grid-cell count to cap
# how far any entity can be dragged/nudged/placed. Left unset here on
# purpose - falls back to the screen-resolution-derived bound (this
# file's original, pre-existing behavior) until you pick real numbers.
# GRID | map_cols | 40
# GRID | map_rows | 25

# move_view_range - real, per-house config for tp_arm_placer_rmmv.+x's
# placing grid (direct live report 2026-09-26: a full-screen grid is
# "inconvenient when using the computer, clicking other things on
# screen"). Cells visible in each direction from an origin (an entity's
# own desktop_pos.txt, when TP_ORIGIN_X/Y are set) before the grid
# window is limited - 0 means unbounded/the old full-screen behavior.
# Uncomment to change; default (built into the binary) is 3.
# GRID | move_view_range | 3

# place_confirm - "double_click" (default, real): a click moves the
# target square, same as an arrow key, and a second click on the SAME
# cell (or Enter) places it. "single_click": the old behavior, any
# click places immediately. Uncomment to opt back into single_click.
# GRID | place_confirm | double_click
